  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration is scVI_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (config_005, acc 0.650), clearly outperforming PCA (0.591) and scGPT (0.530) under the same setup. Image-only with ResNet50 is very weak (0.208), raising the question of whether image features add any complementary signal in a multimodal setting. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether fusing image features with the strong scVI_n200 RNA representation helps or hurts performance. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests whether adding the image modality to the best RNA configuration provides a benefit, using the simplest fusion (concat) and the aggregation (avgpool) already shown to be superior to transformer. This is the best use of the next slot because: (1) it isolates the effect of adding image features to the current best model, (2) if it helps, the remaining 3 experiments can optimize the multimodal setup (e.g., try ViT-L or weighted fusion); if it does not help, the remaining budget can focus on RNA-only refinements, and (3) it changes only one design dimension (adding image + fusion) relative to the proven best RNA config, keeping the comparison clean."
}

